Why Is FD-SOI Technology Becoming Important for Advanced Semiconductor Manufacturing?

FD-SOI is a semiconductor transistor technology that uses a thin silicon layer positioned above an insulating layer. This structure improves electrostatic control and helps reduce leakage current, making it suitable for applications where energy efficiency and predictable performance are important.

One of the major advantages of FD-SOI is its body-bias capability. Manufacturers and chip designers can adjust transistor characteristics to balance performance and power consumption according to application requirements.

Unlike advanced FinFET and gate-all-around technologies that primarily target high-density computing, FD-SOI addresses applications requiring a combination of low power, analog integration, RF performance and long product lifecycles.

The technology is particularly relevant to automotive electronics, wireless devices, industrial controllers and intelligent edge systems. These applications require reliable processing capabilities without the high power consumption associated with more demanding computing architectures.

Automotive ADAS Is Emerging as a Major Market Growth Driver

Automotive electronics are becoming increasingly sophisticated as vehicles incorporate advanced driver-assistance systems, radar sensors, electronic control units and connected technologies.

These systems require semiconductor components capable of operating reliably under demanding temperature and power conditions. FD-SOI offers a combination of low leakage, RF integration, body-bias control and automotive-qualified process options that can support these requirements.

Automotive radar is an important application area. GlobalFoundries and indie Semiconductor have collaborated on 22FDX-based radar system-on-chip development targeting 77 GHz and 120 GHz applications.

The collaboration demonstrates how FD-SOI technology can support advanced sensing and vehicle electronics while integrating digital processing and RF-related functions.

As vehicle manufacturers increase investment in ADAS and intelligent mobility platforms, demand for specialized semiconductor manufacturing processes is expected to create additional opportunities for FD-SOI foundries.

